WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
Could you parallel park in a space that is only one centimeter longer than your car?

00:05.660 --> 00:10.460
Mathematically, yes. As long as the gap is even slightly longer than your vehicle,

00:10.820 --> 00:14.640
you can always park, if you are willing to shuffle back and forth enough times.

00:15.240 --> 00:19.680
Here is how the geometry works. By tracking the midpoint between your rear wheels,

00:20.000 --> 00:25.600
every forward and backward pass traces two opposite circular arcs, nudging the car slightly

00:25.600 --> 00:31.460
closer to the curb each time. Just remember one crucial rule from the math. You always

00:31.460 --> 00:35.700
have to finish by reversing, so your front bumper never swings out over the pavement.

